From: Daniel Wagner <dwagner@suse.de>
Subject: kabi: nvdimm/btt: kABI fixup for BTT lane acquisition preemption handling
References: CVE-2026-74365 bsc#1278225
Patch-mainline: Never (kABI fixup)

kABI fix for upstream commit 8d4b989d9c9a ("nvdimm/btt: Handle preemption
in BTT lane acquisition")

nd_region_acquire_lane()/nd_region_release_lane() are EXPORT_SYMBOL and
struct nd_region is reachable from their prototypes, so replacing the
per-CPU spinlock-recursion lane model (struct nd_percpu_lane) with a
per-lane mutex array (struct nd_lane) changes their CRC even though the
lane field stays a single pointer-sized member.
Users are _not_ supposed to synchronize the lane directly bypassing those
exported functions.

Keep genksyms looking at the original struct nd_percpu_lane pointer
type while the compiler builds the real struct nd_lane based code.

Signed-off-by: Daniel Wagner <dwagner@suse.de>
Acked-by: Michal Koutný <mkoutny@suse.com>

---
 drivers/nvdimm/nd.h |   10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/nvdimm/nd.h
+++ b/drivers/nvdimm/nd.h
@@ -365,6 +365,12 @@ unsigned sizeof_namespace_label(struct n
 	for (res = (ndd)->dpa.child, next = res ? res->sibling : NULL; \
 			res; res = next, next = next ? next->sibling : NULL)
 
+#ifdef __GENKSYMS__
+struct nd_percpu_lane {
+	int count;
+	spinlock_t lock;
+};
+#endif
 enum nd_label_flags {
 	ND_LABEL_REAP,
 };
@@ -419,7 +425,11 @@ struct nd_region {
 	struct kernfs_node *bb_state;
 	struct badblocks bb;
 	struct nd_interleave_set *nd_set;
+#ifdef __GENKSYMS__
+	struct nd_percpu_lane __percpu *lane;
+#else
 	struct nd_lane *lane;
+#endif
 	int (*flush)(struct nd_region *nd_region, struct bio *bio);
 	struct nd_mapping mapping[] __counted_by(ndr_mappings);
 };
